<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Clients, Scripts, Triggers and Bots</h1>
<p>First, what the words mean:
</p>
<ul><li><b>Alias</b>: a short cut to one or more commands (see <a cmd='#'>Help Alias</a>).</li>
<li><b>Trigger</b>: an action that activates on output from the mud (see <a cmd='#'>Help Triggers</a>).</li>
<li><b>Script</b> or <b>bot</b>: a program that controls a character without anyone at the screen.</li></ul>
<p>All of them are allowed on Valhalla: you may use aliases and triggers, 
run a script or a bot, and play more than one character at a time. The 
mud's own helpers, such as Dwili and Groa, are bots too.
</p><p>The one rule is that you don't ruin the game for other players. When a 
character, played by hand or by a program, spoils the game for others, 
the gods will step in, as with any other rule (see <a cmd='#'>Help Rules</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Rules</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Alias</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Triggers</a>
</pre>




</div>